    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's more than just research to me though. the timing is too precise. it's like the building knows when i'm actually winding down for the night, and that's right when the frequency ramps up the most. it feels less like an \"experiment\" and more like a controlled compliance mechanism for the residents. if this were actually being implemented as a behavioral tool, how would they hide the signal so that standard building diagnostics wouldn't flag it as an anomaly?",
